---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const AM = "server/src/iki_server/amounts";
const SVC = `${AM}/services.py`;
const ELIG = `${AM}/eligibility.py`;
const SAMPLE = "plugins/samples/types/sample.yaml";

const H = {
  short: "Taking material for work",
  how: "What a draw checks, the scan, samples and lot draws",
  example: "A tube drawn for an assay",
  rules: "Purposes, holds and draw targets in full",
  ref: "Code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "checks", label: "What a draw checks" },
  { id: "scan", label: "Scanning the tube" },
  { id: "samples", label: "Samples" },
  { id: "lots", label: "Drawing from a lot" },
  { id: "example", label: H.example },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A draw uses material up: a <code>drawn</code> movement on the tube or lot, with a purpose
      (routine use or QA sampling) and, usually, the record it went into. Before it's written, the
      server locks the records, checks holds and draw guards on the record and on what it follows,
      the purpose's lab roles, a scan when the type asks for one, and the balance. A sample is a
      portion drawn for identified work: it names its source, accepts exactly one matched draw from
      it, and keeps a receipt of that draw. The sample has no balance of its own; the ledger is the
      record of what was taken (<Adr n={[139, 180, 211]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="checks">What a draw checks</h3>
    <p>
      <code>POST /entities/&#123;ref&#125;/amount/draw</code> needs an Editor of the record's project,
      or a reader of it who is an Editor of the project whose container holds it, and an Editor of
      the record it's used in. Under the locks, a draw
      is refused while a state holds the record's amount, such as a lot's quarantine on a type that
      says so; while one of its draw guards fails; while a record it follows is held or fails its own
      guards; or when it asks for more than there is (<Path p={SVC} sym="def draw(" />, <Path
        p={SVC}
        sym="def _taking("
      />, <Path p={ELIG} sym="def refusals(" />). A tube's own guards:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/inventory/types/tube.yaml" start="^draw_guards:" />
    <p>
      The tube follows its <code>contents</code>, so a lot in it brings the lot's guards to the
      bench. They read the draw's <code>purpose</code> and <code>operation</code>, so a quarantined
      lot gives only QA sampling:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/lots/types/lot.yaml" start="^draw_guards:" />
    <p>
      A type's <code>draw_purposes</code> names the lab roles that may draw for each purpose; the
      lot's QA sampling needs Lot QA (<Path p={ELIG} sym="def purpose_refusals(" />). Putting a tube on
      hold needs a reason, and an inventory trigger can put the tubes split or transferred from it on
      hold too (<Path p="plugins/inventory/triggers/hold_derived_tubes.yaml" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="scan">Scanning the tube</h3>
    <p>
      A type whose <code>storage.confirm</code> lists <code>draw</code>, as the tube's does, needs a
      scan of the record before a draw. The code is resolved among what the caller can read: an Iki
      label's <code>IKI:</code> code, a record link, an HRID or the vendor's barcode, and it must name
      the record being drawn from. The code is kept on the movement as <code>confirmed</code> (<Path
        p={SVC}
        sym="def _confirmed("
      />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/storage/scan_identity.py" sym="class ScanIndex:" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="samples">Samples</h3>
    <p>
      An <code>iki/samples.Sample</code> is made pending, with an immutable source, a tube or a lot,
      and the work it's for: a record such as a request or a plate, or a run.
      Its <code>draw_target</code> makes it take one matched draw while it awaits material, and
      its <code>draws_received</code> field keeps the receipt (<Adr n="0211" />):
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={SAMPLE} start="^draw_target:" />
    <p>
      The draw names the sample as <code>used_in</code>. It's refused unless the sample is pending,
      has no draw yet, and the draw is from its assigned source (<Path
        p={SVC}
        sym="def _check_draw_target("
      />). In the same transaction the sample's receipt gains the movement, the debited record and its
      revision, the source it followed and that one's revision, the amount and unit, the operator and
      the time (<Path p={SVC} sym="def _receive_draw(" />). Setting it to Received needs that one draw;
      testing, a signed submission and an independent signed review follow:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file={SAMPLE} start="^      received:" />
    <p>
      How a returned result on a sample counts toward a request is on <PageLink
        to="Release and completion"
        hash="completion"
      />.
    </p>

    <h3 id="lots">Drawing from a lot</h3>
    <p>
      A sample whose source is a lot is drawn directly from the lot's balance, in the lot's own units
      and under its own guards and purposes. A tube holding the lot is a different source: a draw from
      it debits the tube, and the lot is the source it followed (<Adr n="0211" />, <Path
        p="plugins/lots/types/lot.yaml"
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={3} title={H.example}>
    <p>
      For an assay, a scientist draws 50 µL from a tube with <code
        >POST /api/v1/entities/&#123;tube&#125;/amount/draw</code
      >, naming the experiment it's used in and scanning the tube. The server locks the tube, the
      experiment and the lot the tube follows, checks the tube's guards and the lot's, the scan and the
      balance, and appends a <code>drawn</code> movement with its purpose and the lot as its source.
      The experiment's own <code>draws_received</code> field records the draw, and the graph gains
      a <code>used</code> edge from the experiment to the tube (<Adr n="0189" />, <Path
        p="plugins/experiments/types/experiment.yaml"
      />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Draw purposes" open>
        <p>
          A draw's purpose is <code>routine</code> or <code>qa_sampling</code>; the database requires
          one on every <code>drawn</code> movement and none on any other (<Path
            p={`${AM}/models.py`}
            sym="class DrawPurpose("
          />). A guard can read the purpose, and the type's <code>draw_purposes</code> narrows who may
          draw for each.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="What a draw follows">
        <p>
          <code>follows</code> names references, and the first that's set is the draw's source. A
          record's guards are checked with those of what it follows, three levels deep, and a followed
          record a state holds refuses the draw by name (<Path p={ELIG} sym="def followed(" />). When the
          draw goes into a draw target or a record with <code>draws_received</code>, the followed
          records are locked too, and a source that changed during the draw makes it retry.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Draw targets">
        <p>
          A <code>draw_target</code> names the field holding the container to draw from, optionally the
          source it must follow, the state that means it's awaiting material, the lab roles the person drawing needs, a field
          that must be set first, whether the container must be in storage, and a planned amount the
          draw must match exactly (<Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/model.py" sym="class DrawTarget:" />). A
          stability pull is the other draw target <code>iki</code> ships (<PageLink
            to="Receipts and counts"
            hash="pulls"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={SVC} sym="def draw(" />: the draw, its checks and its receipt</li>
        <li><Path p={ELIG} />: holds, draw guards and purposes</li>
        <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/storage/scan_identity.py" />: what a scanned code names</li>
        <li><Path p="plugins/samples" />: the sample, its draw and its review</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0139" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0180" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0189" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0211" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
